gosity":"heterozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"nonsense","key":"V5"}],"variant_roles":["causal","causal"],"segregation":"","inheritance":"AR","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["At the age of 5 months, he presented failure to thrive, hypotonia, feeding difficulties, bilateral hearing impairment, pulmonary hypertension, livedo reticularis, and distal phalangeal erythema (Figure 1). Laboratory tests showed anemia, lactic acidosis, 3‐methyl‐glutaconic, and tricarboxylic aciduria and decreased CoQ10 levels in lymphocytes.","biallelic PDSS1 mutations were identified (NM_014317.3: c.716 T > G (p.Val239Gly) and NM_014317.3: c.1183C > T (p.Arg395*))","However, he developed a progressive multisystem disorder with severe developmental delay, pyramidal dysfunction, seizures, tremor, optic atrophy and nystagmus, severe visual and hearing impairment, white matter cystic change and chronic heart failure. He died at the age of 3 years old."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"two different heterozygous variants in one gene"}],"notes":[{"id":"N:34765390:1","pmid":"34765390","section":"clinical_management","statement":"Bellusci et al. (2021) found that oral CoQ10 (ubidecarenone) supplementation, increased from 15 to 30 mg/kg/day, did not control disease progression in a patient with PDSS1-related primary CoQ10 deficiency, who died at 3 years of age.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["Supplementation with high dose of coenzyme Q10 was not effective to control disease progression and the patient died at the age of 3 years old because of a progressive multisystem disorder."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:34765390:2","pmid":"34765390","section":"pathogenesis","statement":"Bellusci et al. (2021) suggested that the coexistence of distal phalangeal erythema, livedo reticularis, and pulmonary hypertension in a patient with PDSS1 mutations pointed to microvascular dysfunction as a possible underlying mechanism.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["The coexistence in our case of phalangeal erythema, livedo reticularis, and pulmonary hypertension suggests microvascular dysfunction as a possible underlying physiopathogenic mechanism."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:33285023:1","pmid":"33285023","section":"clinical_features","statement":"Nardecchia et al. (2021) noted that in PDSS1 deficiency, unlike OPA1 and OPA3 defects, sensorineural deafness seemed to precede optic atrophy, and proposed that PDSS1 deficiency, a potentially treatable condition, be included in the differential diagnosis of optic atrophy with sensorineural deafness.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["In contrast to OPA1 and OPA3 defects, the onset of sensorineural deafness seems to precede the optic atrophy in PDSS1, hallmarking this particular form.","CoQ10 synthesis defects should be deemed as treatable conditions and as such should enter in the differential diagnosis of optic atrophy and sensorineural deafness, although ultrarare so far."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:33285023:2","pmid":"33285023","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"Nardecchia et al. (2021) found that the PDSS1 Q245H variant affected a highly conserved residue (98.5% conservation across 184 eukaryotic sequences), was absent from gnomAD, and lay within a 12-Mb region of homozygosity.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["This variant causes the amino acid change p.Gln245His, in a highly conserved position (98.5%, Fig. 1A). The variant lies in a long region of homozygosity (12 Mb)"],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:33285023:3","pmid":"33285023","section":"genotype_phenotype_correlations","statement":"Nardecchia et al. (2021) noted that visual involvement in CoQ10 deficiencies had been reported only with defects in the first steps of CoQ10 synthesis: optic atrophy in PDSS1 deficiency, optic atrophy with retinitis pigmentosa in PDSS2 deficiency, and retinitis pigmentosa alone in COQ2 deficiency.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["Visual system involvement in CoQ10 deficiencies has been reported only in the defect of the very first steps of CoQ10 synthesis and it consists of optic atrophy, a combination of optic atrophy and retinitis pigmentosa or retinitis pigmentosa only in PDSS1, PDSS2, and COQ2 defect, respectively."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:22494076:1","pmid":"22494076","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"Vasta et al. (2012) performed targeted next-generation sequencing of the exons of 908 known and candidate nuclear genes in 26 patients with known or suspected mitochondrial disorders. Among the variants identified in known pathogenic genes were variants in PDSS1, along with variants in CPT2, POLG, UBE3A, and SDHD.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["Targeted next-generation sequencing was performed on 26 patients with known or suspected mitochondrial disorders using in-solution capture for the exons of 908 known and candidate nuclear genes and an Illumina genome analyzer.","Instead, several variants in known pathogenic genes including CPT2, POLG, PDSS1, UBE3A, SDHD, and a few potentially pathogenic variants in candidate genes such as MTO1 or SCL7A13 were identified."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:17332895:1","pmid":"17332895","section":"biochemical_features","statement":"Mollet et al. (2007) found that quinone-dependent OXPHOS activities were in the range of the lowest control values while OXPHOS enzyme activities were normal; CoQ10 deficiency was confirmed by restoration of normal OXPHOS activities after addition of quinone.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["CoQ10 deficiency was confirmed by restoration of normal OXPHOS activities after addition of quinone."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:17332895:2","pmid":"17332895","section":"mapping","statement":"Mollet et al. (2007) performed a genome-wide search for homozygosity in family 1 and identified a region of chromosome 10 encompassing the PDSS1 gene.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["A genome-wide search for homozygosity in family 1 identified a region of chromosome 10 encompassing the gene prenyldiphosphate synthase, subunit 1 (PDSS1)"],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:17332895:3","pmid":"17332895","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"Mollet et al. (2007) showed that transformation of a yeast Delta-coq1 strain with mutant yeast COQ1 (corresponding to the PDSS1 D308E mutation) resulted in defective growth on respiratory medium, indicating that the mutation causes the OXPHOS deficiency.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["Transformation of yeast Deltacoq1 and Deltacoq2 strains by mutant yeast COQ1 and mutant human COQ2 genes, respectively, resulted in defective growth on respiratory medium, indicating that these mutations are indeed the cause of OXPHOS deficiency."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]}],"dropped":{"records":[],"notes":[]},"gene_decisions":{"candidates":["PDSS1","COQ2"],"confirmed":["PDSS1"],"dropped":[],"not_confirmed":["COQ2"]},"candidate_inheritance":["AR"]}